ATTRIBUTION

This project is a TypeScript port of selected parts of mautrix-linkedin
(https://github.com/mautrix/linkedin), a Go-based Matrix↔LinkedIn bridge
licensed under the GNU AGPLv3.

The following modules and constants in src/voyager/ are derived from the
corresponding files under pkg/linkedingo/ in mautrix-linkedin:

  src/voyager/urn.ts            ← pkg/linkedingo/urn.go
  src/voyager/restli.ts         ← pkg/linkedingo/request.go (queriesToString)
  src/voyager/headers.ts        ← pkg/linkedingo/request.go, client.go
  src/voyager/cookies.ts        ← pkg/linkedingo/stringcookiejar.go
  src/voyager/queryIds.ts       ← pkg/linkedingo/constants.go
  src/voyager/realtime.ts       ← pkg/linkedingo/realtime.go
  src/voyager/realtimeMaps.ts   ← pkg/linkedingo/x-li-query-map.json
                                  pkg/linkedingo/x-li-recipe-map.json
  src/voyager/client.ts (api shape and parsing of conversations / messages /
                         send) ← pkg/linkedingo/conversations.go, messages.go,
                                 self.go

mautrix-linkedin Copyright (C) Tulir Asokan and the mautrix-linkedin
contributors. The mautrix-linkedin LICENSE.exceptions document grants
named exceptions to Beeper and Element; those exceptions do NOT apply to
this project.

The original mautrix-linkedin source remains the canonical reference for
the LinkedIn Voyager protocol; consult it for protocol changes that this
port has not yet picked up.
